# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Volume % Change vs Moving Average (Watchlist Column / Sorting Study)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DESCRIPTION:
#   This study is optimized for use as a custom Watchlist Column in ThinkOrSwim.
#   It outputs the percentage volume change compared to the 50-day average.
#   
#   Since it defines exactly one plot (as required by TOS Custom Quotes),
#   you can add this column to your Watchlist and click the header to sort 
#   your watchlist by volume spikes.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

input maLength = 50;

def avgVol = Average(volume, maLength);

# The single plot allowed for custom Watchlist columns (rounded to 1 decimal place)
plot VolPctChange = if avgVol != 0 then Round(100 * (volume - avgVol) / avgVol, 1) else 0;

# Dynamic text color (Green for positive, Red for negative)
VolPctChange.AssignValueColor(if VolPctChange >= 0 then Color.GREEN else Color.RED);

# Optional: Dark green background for spikes >= 100% (double average volume)
AssignBackgroundColor(if VolPctChange >= 100 then CreateColor(0, 50, 0) else Color.CURRENT);
